# Release packages.
#
# The hammerspoonX.Y.Z.zip handed over for each release is a BUILD
# ARTIFACT, not a source file. Committing it would put a ~1.4M binary in
# the history for every release while adding nothing `git checkout`
# cannot already reproduce. (Until 6.162.0 snippets/ was the exception;
# now the public packs are committed under hammerspoon/packs/ and the
# table is rebuilt from them on any machine.)
#
# 🚨 THE ZIP HAS init.lua AT ITS ROOT, WITH NO WRAPPER FOLDER. This
# recipe used to build one and contradicted INSTALL.md Step 3, which
# tells you to unzip into a folder and then run
# `<that folder>/tools/hs-install.sh <that folder>` — a wrapper puts
# everything one level down and both halves of that instruction miss.
#
# 🚨 SINCE 6.117.0 THE ZIP CARRIES snippets/bundled.lua AND NOT THE .json
# PACKS IT WAS BUILT FROM. text_expander.lua does not read the packs when
# the table loads. SINCE 6.162.0 the packs it is built from are the
# COMMITTED hammerspoon/packs/ (1,926 public snippets in four
# collections) plus anything private left in the gitignored snippets/;
# textpanders is neither — it lives in LL's OneDrive snippets folder.
#
# To rebuild any release from source:
#   git checkout <the tag or commit for that version>
#   mkdir -p /tmp/pkg
#   lua5.4 hammerspoon/tools/build-snippets.lua hammerspoon           ← builds the table
#   lua5.4 hammerspoon/tools/build-feature-list.lua hammerspoon       ← 6.217.0: RESOLVED-FEATURE-REQUESTS.txt
#   lua5.4 hammerspoon/tools/build-test-plan.lua hammerspoon          ← 6.271.0: TESTING.md
#   cp -R hammerspoon/init.lua hammerspoon/core hammerspoon/modules \
#         hammerspoon/tools hammerspoon/tests hammerspoon/snippets \
#         hammerspoon/GUIDE.md hammerspoon/INSTALL.md hammerspoon/HAMSIDIAN.md \
#         hammerspoon/CHANGELOG.md hammerspoon/RESOLVED-FEATURE-REQUESTS.txt \
#         hammerspoon/TESTING.md /tmp/pkg/
#   lua5.4 hammerspoon/tools/build-snippets.lua hammerspoon --check   ← REQUIRED
#   find /tmp/pkg/snippets -mindepth 1 -depth ! -name bundled.lua -delete
#   (cd /tmp/pkg && zip -qr ../hammerspoonX.Y.Z.zip .)
#
# Always run tools/run-tests.sh from INSIDE the unpacked package before
# handing it over — that checks what actually ships, not what happens to
# be sitting in the working tree.
hammerspoon*.zip

# macOS Finder droppings, in case the repo is ever opened on the Mac
# itself rather than only being installed to ~/.hammerspoon from it.
.DS_Store

# 📦 THE CURRENT RELEASE ARCHIVE IS UN-IGNORED **AND COMMITTED** (6.263.0),
# and since 6.266.0 it is a **.tar.gz, not a .zip**.
#
# The committing came first, on evidence: the release was delivered twice
# with the file untracked — once gitignored, once merely un-ignored — and
# both times LL got nothing he could open. Tracked was the one variable
# never tried. IT WAS TRIED, AND 6.265.0 ARRIVED EMPTY TOO ("265 was an
# empty zip. I'm honestly tired of fixing that."), which spent the last
# variable inside that pipeline. So the format and the transport both
# changed:
#   · tar.gz — a different writer here, a different unpacker on his Mac,
#     and macOS opens it on a double-click exactly as it opens a .zip;
#   · committed AND LINKED, so his browser → GitHub → Downloads is a
#     second, entirely separate way to get the same bytes.
# ONE AT A TIME: the previous release's archive is deleted in the same
# commit, so the working tree carries exactly one. The COST is real and
# named in CLAUDE.md — git history keeps every blob for ever, ~3 MB a
# release.
#
#   (cd /tmp/pkg && tar -czf ../hammerspoonX.Y.Z.tar.gz .)
#   tar -tzf hammerspoonX.Y.Z.tar.gz | wc -l     ← entries
#   tar -xzf hammerspoonX.Y.Z.tar.gz -C /tmp/verify && sed -n 7p /tmp/verify/init.lua
#
hammerspoon*.tar.gz
# 🚨 THE UN-IGNORE IS PINNED TO A VERSION, SO IT GOES STALE SILENTLY —
# and it had. It still named 6.275.0 five releases later, which means
# every archive since was committed only because it was force-added by
# hand, and the first release that forgot would have shipped a commit
# with no archive in it and nothing saying so. MOVE THIS LINE IN THE
# SAME COMMIT THAT BUILDS THE ARCHIVE, exactly as the previous one is
# deleted there (ONE AT A TIME, above).
!hammerspoon6.293.0.tar.gz
